# Build context of deploy/images/platform.Dockerfile, which is the repository root. BuildKit reads
# this file instead of a .dockerignore at the root.
#
# Only what `uv sync --package ais0c-worker --package ais0c-api` needs gets in (uv reads every
# workspace member's pyproject.toml to check uv.lock, and builds the two services and the
# workspace packages they depend on), plus the approved content the image carries. Docs, tests,
# config/litellm, deploy files, .env and local secrets stay out.
*
!.python-version
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!harness/pyproject.toml
!packages/*/pyproject.toml
!services/*/pyproject.toml
!packages/*/src
!services/worker/src
!services/api/src
!config/agents
!config/models
!prompts
!skills
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
